From a6f782db9c26f476abb018126495fa2061e5c7b5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yaegerbomb42 <yaeger.james42@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 12:57:35 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] feat(ui): live browser view polls run screenshot frames

Replaces the static browser placeholder with a real view of the run's
headless Chromium session: the frame route
(/api/runtime/browser/[runId]/frame) is polled at a modest 1s cadence
while the tab is visible (pausing when hidden, with exponential backoff
on errors), and frame-bearing SSE events (browser.frame /
browser.navigated) trigger an immediate refetch. The address bar tracks
the run's current URL, refused navigations surface a "blocked by policy"
notice, and a waiting state is shown before the first frame exists.

The polling schedule is extracted into pure helpers
(browserPollSchedule / nextBrowserPollDelayMs / recordBrowserPollOutcome)
and unit-tested for interval, backoff, cap, and reset behavior.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
